# Shell scripts must stay LF even in a Windows checkout.
#
# EAS uploads the working tree rather than the git tree, so whatever git wrote
# to disk is what runs on the build machine. A CRLF checkout turns the first
# line into `set -euo pipefail\r`, and bash rejects it:
#
#   set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# The same upload path is why the executable bit cannot be relied on either -
# the CI configs invoke these through `bash <script>` for that reason.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Normalise text in the repository, and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.wasm binary
*.gz binary
*.br binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
*.apk binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
